            <ArticleTitle>[Potential applications of beta-elemene in anti-atherosclerosis and anti-restenosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>656-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is well known that beta-elemene is a broadly effective antitumor drug. In recent years, many studies suggested that beta-elemene also has potential value in the treatment of atherosclerosis and restenosis. In this paper, the effect of beta-elemene in inhibition of angiogenesis, inhibition of thrombus formation, improvement of hemorheology, protection against oxidative injuries, anti-inflammation and suppression of restenosis after percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) are summarized and reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
